# The exact bytes of a corpus file ARE the test.
#
# Without this, git's end-of-line normalisation rewrites `assets/crlf.md` to LF
# on checkout and the case silently stops testing anything — on every machine
# except the one that wrote it. The same normalisation, and the same silence,
# threatens every BOM, UTF-16 and binary fixture here.
#
# `-text` means: never guess, never convert, store and restore these byte for
# byte. It is the right default for a corpus, where a fixture that arrives
# subtly different is worse than one that fails to arrive at all.
* -text
